["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"aep","stream_identity":"01a0d3bf-067c-7068-af65-bd964ce78fcb","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"story","fields":{"body":"# Story: The website's version claims are generated from the tag\n\n## Outcome\n\nA visitor to the front page is told which version this is, and it is right. When this was filed\n`website/src/pages/index.tsx` showed a chip reading `0.7.1-infra-waves-1-4` — twenty-six tags behind\nwhat was live — and that is the first version number any visitor ever sees.\n\n## Context\n\nThe site makes claims about the repository that the repository can answer, and each was typed by\nhand, so each had drifted by a different amount. Measured 2026-08-30, at 0.33.0:\n\n| where | said | behind |\n|---|---|---|\n| `website/src/pages/index.tsx` release chip | `0.7.1-infra-waves-1-4` | 26 tags |\n| `website/docs/status/where-this-stands.md` currency line | as of the tag `0.32.1` | 1 tag |\n| `website/docs/status/where-this-stands.md` gate line | `task check` runs **twenty steps** | correct on the day, wrong the next time a step lands |\n\n**One candidate was examined and rejected.** `website/docs/status/limitations.md:34` reads *\"Two\ndurable backends implement the contract, as of `0.27.0`\"*. That is not a stale stamp — it is a\nhistorical fact about **when** something became true, and rewriting it to the newest tag would make\nit say something false. It stays hand-written. The distinction is the whole point: a generator that\ncannot tell a currency claim from a *since* claim would have corrupted this line on its first run.\n\nThe repository already solved this once, in the same words: `docs/status.md`'s delivered-waves table\nis generated by `cargo xtask status` from the annotated tags, and `status-check` fails when it\ndrifts. Nothing in that mechanism is specific to `docs/status.md` — it is a marked region, a\ngenerator and a `--check`.\n\nThe gate-step line joined the story after the fact, and belongs to it: it is the same class of\nclaim, it went wrong the moment `docs-check` landed\n(`story:cli-reference-covers-every-verb`), and it is derivable from `Taskfile.yml`'s own `check:`\nblock. A stamp mechanism that leaves the neighbouring sentence hand-written has not finished.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- The three claims above sit in generated regions written by `cargo xtask status` — the tag and its\n  date from the newest tag reachable from `HEAD`, the step list from `Taskfile.yml`.\n- `cargo xtask status --check` fails when a region no longer matches, so `status-check` — already\n  the second step of `task check` — covers the website.\n- Nothing is added to the release procedure. `AGENTS.md` § *Releases* already runs\n  `cargo xtask status` after the tag exists and commits what it wrote.\n- A stamp edited by hand turns the gate red, proven by a test that edits one.\n- `limitations.md`'s *since* claim is untouched.\n","document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"ent-63a0b85eb608b0664a69ae8fcc1f551d","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/website-version-stamps-are-generated","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":5,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"# Story: The website's version claims are generated from the tag\n\n## Outcome\n\nA visitor to the front page is told which version this is, and it is right. When this was filed\n`website/src/pages/index.tsx` showed a chip reading `0.7.1-infra-waves-1-4` — twenty-six tags behind\nwhat was live — and that is the first version number any visitor ever sees.\n\n## Context\n\nThe site makes claims about the repository that the repository can answer, and each was typed by\nhand, so each had drifted by a different amount. Measured 2026-08-30, at 0.33.0:\n\n| where | said | behind |\n|---|---|---|\n| `website/src/pages/index.tsx` release chip | `0.7.1-infra-waves-1-4` | 26 tags |\n| `website/docs/status/where-this-stands.md` currency line | as of the tag `0.32.1` | 1 tag |\n| `website/docs/status/where-this-stands.md` gate line | `task check` runs **twenty steps** | correct on the day, wrong the next time a step lands |\n\n**One candidate was examined and rejected.** `website/docs/status/limitations.md:34` reads *\"Two\ndurable backends implement the contract, as of `0.27.0`\"*. That is not a stale stamp — it is a\nhistorical fact about **when** something became true, and rewriting it to the newest tag would make\nit say something false. It stays hand-written. The distinction is the whole point: a generator that\ncannot tell a currency claim from a *since* claim would have corrupted this line on its first run.\n\nThe repository already solved this once, in the same words: `docs/status.md`'s delivered-waves table\nis generated by `cargo xtask status` from the annotated tags, and `status-check` fails when it\ndrifts. Nothing in that mechanism is specific to `docs/status.md` — it is a marked region, a\ngenerator and a `--check`.\n\nThe gate-step line joined the story after the fact, and belongs to it: it is the same class of\nclaim, it went wrong the moment `docs-check` landed\n(`story:cli-reference-covers-every-verb`), and it is derivable from `Taskfile.yml`'s own `check:`\nblock. A stamp mechanism that leaves the neighbouring sentence hand-written has not finished.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- The three claims above sit in generated regions written by `cargo xtask status` — the tag and its\n  date from the newest tag reachable from `HEAD`, the step list from `Taskfile.yml`.\n- `cargo xtask status --check` fails when a region no longer matches, so `status-check` — already\n  the second step of `task check` — covers the website.\n- Nothing is added to the release procedure. `AGENTS.md` § *Releases* already runs\n  `cargo xtask status` after the tag exists and commits what it wrote.\n- A stamp edited by hand turns the gate red, proven by a test that edits one.\n- `limitations.md`'s *since* claim is untouched.\n","owner":"docs","relations":[{"serves":"vision:O2"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"The three typed version claims on the site become generated regions written by cargo xtask status; the front page is 26 tags stale today.","tags":["docs","gate"],"title":"The website's version claims are generated from the tag, not typed"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"},"owner":"docs","relations":[{"serves":"vision:O2"}],"summary":"The three typed version claims on the site become generated regions written by cargo xtask status; the front page is 26 tags stale today.","tags":["docs","gate"],"title":"The website's version claims are generated from the tag, not typed"},"id":"ent-63a0b85eb608b0664a69ae8fcc1f551d","lifecycle_state":"implemented","revision":5,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["story","ent-63a0b85eb608b0664a69ae8fcc1f551d"]}]